{
  "$comment": "DRAFT Sierra Leonean Krio red-flag rules (FR-05, PRD 9.1 layer 1). NOT CLINICALLY APPROVED and NOT YET REVIEWED BY A NATIVE SPEAKER: seed list for the local demo only. English rules (en.json) and the Pidgin/Patois lists always run as well, so this file only adds Krio wording. Matching rules are the same as en.json (normalised text, whole words; see en.json $comment). Krio is written both in the standard orthography (ɛ, ɔ) and informally with e/o, so patterns accept both. 'blo' means breathe but also blow (blo nos = blow your nose), so the breathing rule excludes 'blo ... nos'. 'day' means die.",
  "language": "kri",
  "kind": "language",
  "status": "DRAFT_NOT_CLINICALLY_APPROVED",
  "reviewed": false,
  "rules": [
    {
